Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Principal seam, Tee, Exchange record, Capture sink, Memory bound, Redaction, Logs; AC8, AC22, AC24, supports AC7, AC12, AC29)
Why this approach: capture hangs off the three hooks 001 already owns (ServeHTTP wraps the writer, Rewrite wraps the body as watcher(tee(body)) and snapshots the upstream headers, Settle finishes the exchange), so nothing new sits on the byte path. The adapter's SecretDeclarer and ParsingAdapter are read once per proxy. NewProxy keeps 001's signature with capture off; the registry passes WithCapture's Capture to an unexported constructor, so every 001 caller is unchanged. A dropped_memory exchange returns before Submit, so it is counted at that drop site on the process-wide Budget (Budget.Dropped), which already reports Peak for the shutdown line; T16 now logs it with the sink's counts.
Alternatives rejected: a variadic option on NewProxy (not in the plan's interfaces; tests reach the capturing constructor through export_test.go instead); an always-present capture field on proxied lines driven by Protocol (it would break 001's exact-key access-log tests for handlers that set Protocol without a proxy, so the field follows Meta.Capture instead); taking the exchange path from the upstream URL (it carries base_url's path); submitting memory-dropped exchanges to the sink just to count them (they hold no bodies, and it would couple the drop to the queue's capacity); a counter on Capture (copied per proxy, so there would be no single process-wide count).
Trade-off / known limit: AC29 is proven here only on the submitted exchange; its "in the store" half is owned by T14 (subtest in_store of TestRedact_AdapterQueryParams through the real sink and store), recorded in tasks.md and plan.md. The response header snapshot leaves out value-less entries (the anti-sniff Content-Type placeholder), since they are never sent. Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T8").
Verified by: make verify; go test -race over TestCapture_MemoryLimitDrops (over_limit, crosses_limit_mid_stream, each now asserting Budget.Dropped is 1; seen failing with Dropped = 0 against a stub before the counter), TestRedact_AdapterQueryParams, TestCapture_ExchangeFields (non_streamed, streamed, request_incomplete), TestCapture_OutgoingRequestHasNoGetBody/through_proxy, TestAccessLog_CaptureField; request_incomplete and the GetBody guard each proved by breaking the code for a moment and seeing them fail, then reverted. 001's tests pass unchanged.
